[description]

This package provides an in-memory store for [term geo/box] definitions, with memoized calculation
of extended attributes.

[para] The base data is pulled from a backing store, a [package map::box::store::fs] or any other
object providing the API described in section [term {Store API}] of [package map::box::store::fs]. The memory store adds derived attributes, like the perimeter or the
center of a [term geo/box], and the pixel coordinates needed to draw the [term geo/box] on a map at
the various zoom levels. It is the store expected by [package map::box::map-display] and
[package map::box::table-display].

[section API]

[list_begin definitions]

[call [cmd ::map::box::store::memory] [arg storeName] [arg store]]

Creates a new store object named [arg storeName] on top of the backing store [arg store], and
returns the fully qualified name of its command. The [arg storeName] can be [const %AUTO%] to
generate a unique name.

[para] The [arg store] is the name of the command of the backing store, an object providing the
methods [method ids], [method get], and [method visible] as described in section
[term {Store API}] of [package map::box::store::fs]. It is not destroyed together with the memory
store.

[call [arg storeName] [method ids]]

Returns the list of the ids of all [term geo/box]es. This method is delegated to the backing store.

[call [arg storeName] [method visible] [arg geobox]]

Returns the list of the ids of the [term geo/box]es visible in the geographical box [arg geobox].
This method is delegated to the backing store.

[call [arg storeName] [method get] [arg id]]

Returns the attributes of the [term geo/box] with the given [arg id], a dictionary. The attributes
are computed on the first request for an [arg id] and then cached. Throws an error if the [arg id]
is not known to the backing store.

[para] The dictionary contains all
the keys returned by the backing store, i.e. at least [const names] and [const geo] (see
[package map::box::file]), extended with the following derived attributes:

[list_begin definitions]
[def [const center]]
The center of the box, a list of latitude and longitude.

[def [const diameter]]
The length of the diagonal of the box, in meters.

[def [const perimeter]]
The length of the boundary of the box, in meters.
[list_end]

[call [arg storeName] [method pixels] [arg id] [arg zoom]]

Returns the [term geo/box] with the given [arg id] in pixel coordinates of the map at the given
[arg zoom] level, as a point box, i.e. a list of the minimal x, minimal y, maximal x, and maximal y
coordinates (see [package map::slippy]). The result is cached for each combination of [arg id] and
[arg zoom].

[call [arg storeName] [method destroy]]

Destroys the store.

[list_end]

[para] All other methods are delegated to the backing store as well.

[para] The methods [method ids], [method get], [method visible], and [method pixels] are the API
used by [package map::box::map-display]. [package map::box::table-display] uses [method ids] and
[method get], and requires the derived attributes. Any object providing these methods with the
same results can be used in place of a [package map::box::store::memory].

[section EXAMPLE]

[example_begin]
package require map::box::store::fs
package require map::box::store::memory

map box store fs     BoxFiles /path/to/directory
map box store memory Boxes    BoxFiles

foreach id [lb]Boxes ids[rb] {
    set box [lb]Boxes get $id[rb]
    puts "[lb]lindex [lb]dict get $box names[rb] 0[rb]: center [lb]dict get $box center[rb]"
    puts "  at zoom level 15: [lb]Boxes pixels $id 15[rb]"
}
[example_end]

